{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Like a wall</b> — The kaf serves as a comparative prefix before it, and so the meaning is: like a strong tower, so is the name of YHWH for the righteous in time of trouble." "<b>And the wealth of the rich</b> — It seems in his eyes like his fortified city, and he supposes that through it he will be exalted like the righteous through the name, and like a high wall; he imagines his wealth to be in a decorated house. Targum: וישקיף ואסתכי (and he looks and gazes)."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:29.809747595Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}